# Monolith award walk for iomoon -- every position the machine can cash, and
# every mode played, not just announced.
#
# The Monolith (LPA1..LPA10, rules 3.3.3) is a ten-position cycle: EVERY bumper
# hit steps it one place, and entering either scoop with LTB11 or LTB2 lit --
# armed at lane 6 or the Jupiter entry -- cashes whatever it shows.  Each round
# is {lane 6 to arm, one bumper to step, scoop 1 to cash, then play}, twelve
# rounds, which covers all ten positions at least once wherever the cycle
# happens to start without needing to know the position up front.
#
# The play burst after each cash is deliberately the same every round and
# exercises all four timed modes, because which one just started depends on the
# position: 20 bumper hits (Impact Count wants 20 inside its 15 s), both ramps
# (Orbit Flip lights LR12 on Ramp 1 and can drop the ball from Ramp 2), all
# five drop targets (Special Drop Target pays 100,000 each) and both scoops
# (Star Ride pays 10,000,000 and 15,000,000).
#
# The burst is exactly TWENTY bumper hits on purpose.  Bumpers step the
# Monolith, so any multiple of ten leaves the cycle where it was and the
# one-step-per-round walk stays aligned; 20 is the smallest multiple that also
# satisfies Impact Count.
#
# The ten awards, in cycle order:
#   LPA1  Extra Ball        LPA6   9,000,000
#   LPA2  3,000,000         LPA7   Impact Count      (timed, 15 s)
#   LPA3  Little Multiball  LPA8   Orbit Flip        (timed, 15 s)
#   LPA4  6,000,000         LPA9   Special Drop Target
#   LPA5  Special           LPA10  Star Ride
#
# LPA11 / LPA12 (Lagrange Scape / Lagrange Orbit) are not in the cycle and are
# never cashed: the two shooters alternate them (rules 3.3.4), pressed at the end.
#
# Needs a seeded NVRAM with credits -- see dmd/multiball/README.md.
#
# Keys: L lane 6; WEDFG bumpers; LCtrl+H / RCtrl+H scoops; LCtrl+R / RCtrl+R
# ramps; ZXCVN drop targets; LCtrl+- / RCtrl+- shooters.
